                    coach_default:          `A defensible programme is diagnosed, blended to that diagnosis, costed for transfer, and measured. Keep the thread running through all four decisions.`,
                    coach_r1_evidence:      `Good — you traced the symptoms to the underlying gaps before reaching for activities. That diagnosis is the foundation everything else has to defend.`,
                    coach_r1_menu:          `You've jumped to a menu of activities. But what capability gap does each one close? Diagnosis precedes design — design the programme Britannia Severn needs, not the one you like to run.`,
                    coach_r1_sponsor:       `Asking me what I want is flattering, but I hired you for the diagnosis I can't do myself. Trace the silos and slow decisions to the real capability gaps.`,
                    coach_r1_sharp:         `That's the diagnosis I needed: the merger silos as a collective-leadership gap, evidenced and prioritised. Now build the blend to it.`,
                    coach_r1_everything:    `“Fix everything” is not a diagnosis. Trying to close all three gaps fully on £600k dilutes all of them. Choose, and tell me what you're deliberately leaving out.`,
