                    coach_r2_togap:         `You weighted the blend toward the merger-silo collective-leadership gap. The design now actually addresses my number-one problem.`,
                    coach_r2_misblend:      `The blend doesn't lean toward the gap you diagnosed. A self-awareness-heavy design for a silo problem is a mis-blend — match the weight to the diagnosis.`,
                    coach_r2_nosilo:        `You've built almost no collective work, and the silos were the whole reason I called you. Every business unit will still operate alone. Where is the cross-business leadership?`,
                    coach_r2_frontload:     `One intensive week then nine months of silence is how transfer dies. Development has to be sequenced across the journey, not dumped in an offsite.`,
                    coach_r3_balanced:      `You used the full £600k with discipline. Now make sure the mix is weighted to transfer, not just to the budget line.`,
                    coach_r3_didactic:      `Masterclasses for all 120 — it fits with room to spare and the day-one feedback will glow. Then nothing changes, because you can't lecture someone into leading differently. What in this design actually changes behaviour?`,
                    coach_r3_blowout:       `Action-learning for all, coaching for all, bespoke labs — magnificent, and it's well over £600,000. I won't fund 40% over. Where do you scale so the deep formats land where they matter most?`,
                    coach_r3_underspend:    `You've come in well under budget by defaulting to the cheapest formats. That's a false economy — you saved money and bought weak transfer. Spend the budget where behaviour actually changes.`,
                    coach_r3_targeted:      `Smart — coaching and labs reserved where transfer matters most, the rest scaled with peer-coaching and digital. That's transfer-to-practice per pound.`,
                    coach_r3_cheapest:      `Cheapest-for-everyone protects the budget and starves the design of transfer. Coming in under budget isn't the win — changing behaviour is.`,
                    coach_r4_outcome:       `You led with the diagnosis and the transfer logic, format by format. That's the case I can take to the board.`,
                    coach_r4_inspire:       `Energy and great venues are exactly what I'm sceptical of. I'm measuring capability uplift and transfer, not the buzz in the room. Are you designing for the happy sheet or the 9-month review?`,
